<task id="226" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>G1 — per-customer BFF must read its OWN Redis / Service Bus / Storage / OpenAI / DocIntel / AI Search, never `sprksharedprod-*`: verify the live read path, then retire the `from-shared-service` sourcing, H4-shared handler and DAG edge; drop Prompt Flow (D5)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T226 (gap G1 + INCOMING §6 manifest bullet)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <completed-on>2026-09-30</completed-on>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies production `.cs` (handler, DAG, DI registration), the canonical secret manifest + 4 generated artifacts, and tests; tags include `auth` (credential sourcing for data-plane services); root §8 test-modifying override applies.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive (which credential each service uses; ADR-028 A4 secret-free posture) and cross-cutting (manifest generator outputs + DAG + handler retirement + DI + tests). Step 2 is a design decision, not a mechanical change.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <tags>auth, provisioning, l2-controlplane, provisioning-handler, config, testing, d-12, model1-dedicated, secret-catalog</tags>
    <deps>236</deps>
  </metadata>

  <goal>
    After this task, no provisioning run writes, and no per-customer BFF reads, a credential or endpoint belonging to a
    `sprksharedprod-*` resource. For each of the six manifest entries currently sourced `from-shared-service`
    (`Redis-ConnectionString`, `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`, `Storage-ConnectionString`, `AzureOpenAI-ApiKey`,
    `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`) the manifest carries an owner-approved per-customer disposition:
    either (a) **no secret** — the BFF uses the customer UAMI (managed identity) and the entry is omitted on secret-free
    stamps, or (b) **key extracted from the customer's own resource** in `rg-spaarke-{customerId}-prod` and written to the
    customer's own Key Vault. `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` and its DAG edge are retired (H4b depends on H4 only).
    `PromptFlow-Endpoint` / `PromptFlow-Key` are removed from the catalog (D5). `BingSearch-ApiKey` and
    `LlamaParse-ApiKey` stay Spaarke-shared vendor keys (D5), explicitly labelled as such.
  </goal>

