  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4 + .claude/constraints/provisioning.md §KV credential lifecycle (BINDING)">
      Applies to every manifest entry and handler touched in this task: never create/seed/restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret`
      (either casing) or `Dataverse-ClientSecret` in secret-free environments; never purge soft-deleted rollback copies or
      delete the live `Dataverse-ClientSecret` before 2026-11-23; E-1 SpeAdmin secrets untouched. No new
      `.WithClientSecret(...)` / `ClientSecretCredential(...)` on any BFF identity.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="manifest.yaml header (BINDING)">
      Edit `manifest.yaml` only; regenerate the four `generated/` artifacts with `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` and commit
      them atomically with the manifest. Never hand-edit generated output. Generator determinism (byte-identical reruns)
      must hold.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §6 (security-sensitive)">
      The per-secret disposition (MI vs extracted key) is a credential-posture decision. It is proposed in Step 2 and
      APPROVED BY THE OWNER before Step 3 starts. Do not implement a disposition the owner has not approved.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="plan §2 D3">
      Model 2 code paths are not broken. Anything shared between the Model 1 and Model 2 paths keeps working for Model 2.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 + tests/CLAUDE.md">
      Tests for the retired H4-shared handler are deleted WITH the handler (their subject no longer exists). No other
      test is skipped or narrowed; `HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests` count is updated to the new handler count, not
      loosened. ArchTest stays 337/337.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="§10 BFF hygiene">
      This task does not modify `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**`. If Step 2 concludes the BFF itself must change how it
      authenticates to a service, that is a separate BFF task — escalate, do not fold it in.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Step 1 finds a LIVE customer-shaped BFF (any App Service created by a provisioning run) whose app settings
      resolve Redis / Service Bus / Storage / OpenAI / DocIntel / AI Search to a `sprksharedprod-*` resource — report the
      exact settings and STOP before changing anything live (owner directive: do not remediate live envs silently).</trigger>
    <trigger>Step 2 disposition requires the BFF to switch a service from key auth to Entra/MI auth (e.g. Redis) or the
      reverse — that is a BFF change + ADR-028 decision; STOP and present it as a §6.5 choice.</trigger>
    <trigger>Retiring H4-shared breaks a Model 2 path (any Model 2 test or DAG edge depends on it) — STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>ControlPlane.Tests failures exceed the 23-failure task-221 baseline after the change, or ArchTest drops below 337 — STOP and isolate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Modifies existing surfaces (manifest, H4, DAG, KvSecretValueResolver). If Step 2 approves "extract key from the customer's own resource", the existing source-key extractor used by H4-shared (task 200, 5-branch Search/CogSvc/Redis/SB/Storage) is REUSED from H4 — no new extractor.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend H4 + the manifest value_source vocabulary rather than keep a second handler. No new handler is added.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every Model 1 customer's BFF is wired to the same Redis (which caches OBO tokens and the uac-access authorization cache — D-12 §3 reason Redis went per-customer), the same Service Bus and the same AI Search admin key, although `customer.bicep` deploys all six per customer. That is a cross-customer isolation break, not a cost issue.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step n="1" name="Verify the read path (no edits)">
      Trace, with file:line evidence: (a) which Key Vault name H4-shared writes the six secrets to (parameter
      `SharedKeyVaultNameParameterKey` — where does the run get it?); (b) which vault name the per-customer BFF's KV
      references use (`Configure-AppServiceSettings.generated.ps1` + H4b); (c) whether H4 (per-customer) writes any of the
      six, and what it does on secret-free stamps (auth-v4 §9.1 omissions); (d) what `customer.bicep` +
      `bff-runtime-rbac.bicep` already grant the customer UAMI on each of the six services. Read-only `az` checks against
      dev are allowed with the operator's own identity (NFR-11); no writes. Record findings in
      `notes/t226-shared-secret-read-path.md`.
    </step>
    <step n="2" name="Propose per-secret disposition → owner approval">
      For each of the six secrets, propose: MI (omit secret; cite the RBAC grant + the BFF code path that uses MI) or
      extracted key from the customer's own resource (cite why MI is not available, e.g. Redis access-key auth). Present as
      one table via AskUserQuestion / 🔔 Human Input Required. Include Prompt Flow removal and Bing/LlamaParse "Spaarke
      shared vendor key" labelling. Record the approved table in the notes file.
    </step>
    <step n="3" name="Manifest + generator">
      Apply the approved dispositions in `manifest.yaml` (introduce a per-customer value_source only if the approved table
      needs one; teach `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1` + `KvSecretValueResolver` about it). Remove PromptFlow entries. Fix
      the "Not populated on Model1 shared trial" purpose text. Regenerate all four artifacts; verify a second run is
      byte-identical.
    </step>
    <step n="4" name="Retire H4-shared">
      Delete `H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler` and its exclusively-owned types (accessor/source/rejection codes — grep
      each for other consumers first); remove `HandlerIds.H4Shared`, its DI + dispatch registration, and the DAG entry;
      `H4b` depends on `H4` only; update `RunsEndpoints` comments that list H4Shared. If H4 must now extract keys, move
      that logic into H4 reusing the existing extractor.
    </step>
    <step n="5" name="Tests + verification">
      Delete H4-shared tests; update DAG + registration-completeness tests to the new graph; add/adjust H4 tests for any
      new value_source (cover: key extracted from the customer's own resource; secret omitted on a secret-free stamp;
      rejection when the customer resource is missing). Build ControlPlane Api/Worker/Tests; run ArchTests (337/337) and
      ControlPlane.Tests (≤ 23 baseline failures). Grep: zero `sprksharedprod` hits in `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/**`
      and `src/server/services/**`.
    </step>
    <step n="6" name="Quality gates + close">
      Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check. Update this POML (completed + notes), TASK-INDEX row 226, plan §3/§4 status (G1 +
      INCOMING §6 manifest bullet), current-task.md. Commit + push.
    </step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>`notes/t226-shared-secret-read-path.md` records the verified read path (Step 1 a–d, file:line) and the owner-approved per-secret disposition table.</criterion>
    <criterion>`manifest.yaml` has zero `from-shared-service` entries and zero `sprksharedprod` references; the six entries match the approved table; PromptFlow entries removed; Bing + LlamaParse labelled as Spaarke-shared vendor keys.</criterion>
    <criterion>The four `generated/` artifacts are regenerated from the manifest in the same commit; a second generator run produces byte-identical output.</criterion>
    <criterion>`H4SharedKvSecretsPopulationHandler`, `HandlerIds.H4Shared`, its DI/dispatch registration and DAG entry are gone; `DagAdvancer.HandlerDependencies[H4b]` = `{ H4 }`.</criterion>
    <criterion>If any secret is approved as "extracted key", H4 extracts it from the resource in the customer's own RG and writes it to the customer's own KV — tested: happy path, secret-free omission, missing-resource rejection.</criterion>
    <criterion>No new BFF-identity `.WithClientSecret(...)` / `ClientSecretCredential(...)`; KV credential-lifecycle rule untouched (no create/seed/restore of `BFF-API-ClientSecret` / `Dataverse-ClientSecret`).</criterion>
    <criterion>No file under `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**` modified.</criterion>
    <criterion>Builds 0 warn / 0 err; ArchTest 337/337; ControlPlane.Tests failures ≤ 23 (task-221 baseline) with zero new failures.</criterion>
    <criterion>Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check run; findings dispositioned in completion notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

